        <div class="guide-container">
            <h2>How to Install Dev-C++</h2>
            <p style="color: #aebbd0; margin-bottom: 30px;">Follow these simple steps to install Dev-C++ on your Windows PC for C and C++ programming.</p>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 1: Download the Setup</h4>
                <p>Click the "Download Setup" button on the previous page. This will redirect you to the official SourceForge page to download the setup file.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 2: Run the Installer</h4>
                <p>Once the download is complete, double-click the setup file. Allow administrator permissions if prompted by Windows.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 3: Choose Language</h4>
                <p>When the installer opens, select your preferred language (English) and click "OK".</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 4: Accept the License Agreement</h4>
                <p>Read the license agreement and click "I Agree" to proceed.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 5: Choose Components</h4>
                <p>Keep the default components selected and click "Next".</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 6: Select Install Location</h4>
                <p>The default installation folder is fine. Click "Install" to begin the installation process.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-step">
                <h4>Step 7: Finish Installation</h4>
                <p>Once the installation is complete, click "Finish". You can now launch Dev-C++ from your desktop or start menu.</p>
            </div>

